{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Et the three cities.</b> The action is missing here and explained in the section of ואתחנן. Rashi explained here: even though in the land of Canaan there are nine tribes and here there are only two and a half, the number of their cities of refuge was equalized, because in Gilead murderers were numerous, as it is written: ״גלעד קרית פועלי און עקובה מדם״ — that is, even intentional killers flee to cities of refuge, and therefore those in Gilead needed cities of refuge equal to those in the land of Canaan. As is taught in Makkot: בראשון — initially, one unintentional and one intentional — both flee there. בראשון — Rashi explained: at the start of his trial. And that is what is written here: ״ולא ימות הרוצח עד עמדו לפני העדה למשפט״. And so it states in the Sifrei: everyone escorts him to the cities of refuge; the court sends and brings him from there — whoever was liable to death, they executed him, and whoever was not liable to death, they released him."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {0 "The abbreviation פירש״י is resolved as 'פירש רש״י' (Rashi explained); the quotation from Hosea 6:8 is left unaddressed as in the source. The Makkot passage reads בראשון (in the first/mishnaic formulation); the second occurrence of בראשון appears to re-gloss the same term."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:20:47.492305100Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}